From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:25:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] B70-K2-0003: the DFlash draft KV page no longer sets
 the block alone (TP2)

At TP2 the DFlash2 draft holds 8/2 = 4 KV heads per rank, so one draft
sliding-window layer's page (3,407,872 B at block 1664) is 2x the attention
page. With one repeat per group (B70-K2-0002) that page set every KV block,
and every other group padded it to ~50 %: 3.4 MB blocks, 1,170 MiB of state
per running request, KV 77,885 tokens at 3.34 GiB/rank (measured at TP2).

When a sliding-window bucket's groups are wider than every other bucket's
group, split that bucket like a state bucket (as many layers per group as fit
the block, at least one) and, as upstream #60996 does, choose the repeats
per group that minimise the pool bytes a max-length request draws. At TP2
this gives two QSA layers (+ their compressed caches) per group and two GDN
layers per group, one draft layer per group: 36 groups, 3,620,864 B per
block, 663 MiB of state per running request (CPU model: ~221K tokens at the
3.32 GiB/rank measured, vs 78K). TP4 is unchanged: its draft page
(851,968 B) is narrower than a QSA group (905,216 B), so nothing engages.
Token block sizes are untouched (no hash or kernel block change).
B70_KV_DRAFT_PAGE_FIT=0 opts out. Log line "B70-K2-0003" when it engages.

CPU: tests/v1/core/test_b70_kv_pack_repeats.py extended with per-rank TP2
specs (79 passed; the 11 new TP2 checks fail on the previous tree);
test_kv_cache_utils.py + test_contiguous_kv_packing.py: same 4 failures
before and after (pre-existing).
